---
import ChapterLayout from '../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import figure from '../assets/chapters/facilitation-model.png';

const description =
  'Discover the importance of facilitation in collaborative modeling for '
  + 'effective software design. Learn techniques for guiding teams, encouraging '
  + 'ownership, and balancing technical and business perspectives. Explore how '
  + 'social dynamics impact design decisions in our book.';

const figureAlt =
  'A facilitator stands outside a modeling space where a group works at a wall '
  + 'of sticky notes, saying things like “those are not the right boundaries at '
  + 'all”. Below them, in grey, are the thoughts nobody says out loud — “why is '
  + 'nobody listening?”, “how is my cat doing?” — labelled the shadows, the '
  + 'unconsciousness of the group.';
---
<ChapterLayout number="05" title="Facilitating collaborative modeling" description={description}
               figure={figure} figureAlt={figureAlt} figurePlacement="full">
  <p slot="lede">
    Collaborative modeling tools alone do not guarantee effective collaboration;
    someone needs to guide people during collaboration: a facilitator. Fortunately,
    there are techniques and practices you can use to facilitate effective
    collaborative design, whether you’re a project leader, a business stakeholder, or
    an individual technical contributor.
  </p>

  <p>
    We see it as vital for teams to take ownership of their collaborative design
    decisions, a lesson learned from less-than-ideal experiences. We experienced
    frustration when provided with an unrealistic solution by an architect from above
    (in the famous Ivory Tower meme). Our own valuable suggestions, unknown to the
    architect, were overlooked.
  </p>
  <p>
    This book is about looking at software design in a new (or different) way. Enabling
    teams to take ownership of software design and architecture in direct collaboration
    with their stakeholders. Collaborative software design is not just from a technical
    perspective, but also from a business perspective, all whilst taking into account
    the social dynamics that affect both collaborative modeling sessions and design
    decisions. This is what makes this book different.
  </p>
</ChapterLayout>
